//? Title: VAE-GAN: Learned Feature Reconstruction and Isolated Updates
//? Subtitle: Explicit Gaussian codes, a shared generator/discriminator and recomputed D then E then G
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Image reconstruction needs a measure of similarity, while generation must produce an image
from a code alone. Pixel errors can miss useful structure, motivating a learned feature
comparison. This report fits a compact VAE-GAN on 294 local circle/square images, retaining
three parameter groups, three Adam states and 63 visible isolated updates. Four fixed
validation draws select epoch 3 by pixel MSE. Test MC pixel MSE is 0.247712, worse than the
fitting-only mean's 0.048548; all unfiltered reconstruction and prior outputs remain visible.
Feature-target detachment, separate loss equations, first-phase audit and complete editable
C++ distinguish the demonstrated mechanism from an unsupported perceptual-quality claim.
)
\toc

> Learn the comparison, keep the update responsibilities explicit

[Larsen et al. (2016)](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v48/larsen16.html) combine a Gaussian
encoder, a shared decoder/generator and a discriminator whose intermediate features measure
reconstruction. Here E maps 784 pixels through 16 tanh units to four means/log variances.
Explicit epsilon samples z=mu+exp(log_variance/2)*epsilon. G maps z through 16 tanh units to
784 sigmoid probabilities. D maps an image through eight tanh features to one real/fake logit.
The same G processes independent prior codes, and the same D processes all three image kinds.
Only the sampled code reaches G; neither image pixels nor encoder features bypass it.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vae_gan_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(43, 1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle st;
  st.width     = 4.6;
  st.height    = 2.7;
  st.font_size = 20;
  d.node("x", {0, 0}, "Image x\n784 pixels", st)
      .node("e", {6, 0}, "Encoder E\ntanh16 / Gaussian4", st)
      .node("z", {12, 0}, "Posterior code z\nExplicit epsilon", st)
      .node("g", {18, 0}, "Generator G(z)\ntanh16 / sigmoid784", st)
      .node("dr", {24, 0}, "D(reconstruction)\nFeature8 / real logit", st)
      .node("p", {12, 6}, "Independent prior code\nExplicit N(0,I) draw", st)
      .node("gp", {18, 6}, "SAME generator G\nPrior probabilities", st)
      .node("dp", {24, 6}, "SAME D(prior image)\nFeature8 / real logit", st)
      .node("dx", {6, -6}, "SAME D(real x)\nLive real features", st)
      .node("f", {18, -6}, "Feature residual F\nDetach real TARGET", st)
      .edge("x", "e")
      .edge("e", "z")
      .edge("z", "g")
      .edge("g", "dr")
      .edge("p", "gp")
      .edge("gp", "dp")
      .edge("x", "dx")
      .edge("dx", "f")
      .edge("dr", "f")
      .text(
          {12, -11},
          "D then E then G: recompute the forward before each isolated Adam step.\nD stays fixed "
          "during E/G updates; its input Jacobian remains live.",
          20)
      .save_svg("build/vae_gan_method.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/vae_gan_method.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The discriminator serves both real/fake classification and learned feature comparison. The real feature value is detached only inside the reconstruction target; reconstructed-feature paths stay live.)
\alttext(Image encoding supplies a posterior code for G. A separate prior code uses the same G. Reconstructed, prior and real images share D; real and reconstructed features meet at a detached-target feature distance.)

Let f and a denote D's feature vector and logit, and let sp be softplus. Define

$$
F_b=\frac12\sum_j[\operatorname{stop}(f_j(x_b))-f_j(G(z_b))]^2,\qquad
K_b=\frac12\sum_d[\mu_{bd}^2+e^{l_{bd}}-1-l_{bd}],\\
L_E=\operatorname{mean}_b(F_b+K_b),\\
A_G=\frac12[\operatorname{mean}_b\operatorname{sp}(-a(G(z_b)))+
\operatorname{mean}_p\operatorname{sp}(-a(G(z_p)))],\qquad L_G=\operatorname{mean}_b F_b+A_G,\\
L_D=\operatorname{mean}_b\operatorname{sp}(-a(x_b))+
\frac12[\operatorname{mean}_b\operatorname{sp}(a(G(z_b)))+
\operatorname{mean}_p\operatorname{sp}(a(G(z_p)))].
$$
\alttext(The encoder minimizes feature residual plus Gaussian KL. The generator adds two balanced fake-as-real logistic terms. The discriminator classifies real images and two equally weighted fake branches.)

Feature coordinates are summed, and the unit-covariance Gaussian constant is omitted.
Each logistic branch averages its own rows, so the native API allows a different prior batch
size. The report uses matching source batch sizes. These are **three selected objectives**,
not a single pixel-space ELBO. Updating D with the feature loss could collapse its metric;
updating E with the adversarial term would change the specified experiment. The full graph
retains available paths; the caller passes only the intended group's leaves to its optimizer.

This dense teaching variant uses unit feature weight, half-weighted fake branches and a
non-saturating generator loss. It does not reproduce the paper's convolutional architecture,
minimax generator recipe or RMSProp training. Fixed-width forward work is linear in the
number of image/prior rows; dense layers cost O((B+P)[F(H+D)+LH]) for pixel width F, Gaussian
width L, hidden width H and discriminator width D. Activations scale linearly in B+P.

> A loss example small enough to check by hand

Three real features equal to one and reconstructed features equal to zero give F=1.5,
with reconstructed-feature derivatives all -1 and no real-target derivative. For a fully
zeroed small network, sigmoid pixels are 0.5, KL and feature residual are zero, generator
loss is log 2 and discriminator loss is 2 log 2. The three-pixel diagnostic NLL is 3 log 2.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vae_gan_algebra.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  namespace m     = n::models;
  const auto t    = n::DType::Float64;
  auto       real = n::ones({1, 3}, t).requires_grad_(), rec = n::zeros({1, 3}, t).requires_grad_();
  const auto distance = m::VaeGanFeatureNll(real, rec);
  auto       gradient = n::grad(n::sum(distance), {real, rec}, {.allow_unused = true});
  if (distance.item() != 1.5 || gradient[0].defined() ||
      gradient[1].to_vector<double>() != std::vector<double>(3, -1))
    return 1;
  n::ParameterStore e(3301, t), g(3307, t), d(3313, t);
  auto x = n::zeros({2, 3}, t), epsilon = n::zeros({2, 2}, t), prior = n::zeros({3, 2}, t);
  m::VaeGan(e, g, d, x, epsilon, prior, 3, 2, 2, 2);
  for (auto* p : {&e, &g, &d})
    p->unflatten(std::vector<double>(p->count(), 0));
  const auto o = m::VaeGan(e, g, d, x, epsilon, prior, 3, 2, 2, 2);
  if (o.encoder_loss.item() != 0 || std::abs(o.generator_loss.item() - std::log(2.)) > 1e-14 ||
      std::abs(o.discriminator_loss.item() - 2 * std::log(2.)) > 1e-14)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "Feature distance {:.1f}; reconstructed derivatives [-1,-1,-1]; real-target derivative "
      "absent.\n",
      distance.item());
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart
      .bars(
          {0, 1, 2, 3},
          {o.encoder_loss.item(),
           o.generator_loss.item(),
           o.discriminator_loss.item(),
           o.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>()[0]},
          "",
          dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235},
          .6)
      .x_ticks({0, 1, 2, 3}, {"E loss", "G loss", "D loss", "pixel NLL"})
      .title("Zero model / pixel NLL is diagnostic")
      .x_label("separate objectives and one diagnostic")
      .y_label("scalar value / nats")
      .save_svg("build/vae_gan_algebra.svg");
  g.set("output/b", n::full({3}, 1000, t));
  const auto saturated = m::VaeGan(e, g, d, x, epsilon, prior, 3, 2, 2, 2);
  if (saturated.encoder_loss.item() != o.encoder_loss.item() ||
      saturated.generator_loss.item() != o.generator_loss.item() ||
      saturated.discriminator_loss.item() != o.discriminator_loss.item())
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "With zero D fixed, saturated G changes diagnostic pixel NLL from {:.9f} to {:.9f}, while "
      "all three fitted objectives stay unchanged.\n",
      o.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>()[0],
      saturated.pixel_nll.to_vector<double>()[0]);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Feature distance 1.5; reconstructed derivatives [-1,-1,-1]; real-target derivative absent.
With zero D fixed, saturated G changes diagnostic pixel NLL from 2.079441542 to 41.406956968, while all three fitted objectives stay unchanged.
\image(figures/vae_gan_algebra.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The zero-model objectives are separate scalars. The deliberately zero discriminator also gives a controlled case where saturated output pixels worsen pixel NLL without changing the specified training losses.)
\alttext(Bars show E loss zero, G loss log two, D loss twice log two and diagnostic pixel NLL three times log two.)

Pixel NLL clips sigmoid probabilities to the original Float32-represented endpoints 1e-6 and
1-1e-6, even when a caller chooses Float64 computation. It remains a diagnostic: neither
pixel NLL nor pixel MSE appears in any fitted objective. Learned feature error also depends
on the current D, so its magnitude alone does not establish perceptual similarity.

> Native local data and the complete fitting program

Offline native beta-vae-assets preparation enumerates 2 shapes×3 sizes×7 x×7 y=294 binary
28×28 images. Radius is size+2 and centre is (3x+5,3y+5). Circles use inclusive Euclidean
radius; squares use inclusive Chebyshev radius. Residue (x+2y+size+3shape) mod 7 assigns
test=0, validation=1 and fit=2–6, giving 210/42/42 disjoint factor combinations. These are
small structured teaching data. Factor labels never enter the networks or checkpoint criterion.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n      = dm::nn;
  const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets");
  const auto a     = n::load_npz((std::filesystem::path(cache) / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  auto       find  = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  std::print("| pool | images | image geometry | factor columns |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"}) {
    const auto x = find(split + "_images"), f = find(split + "_factors");
    std::print("| {} | {} | 28x28x1 | {} |\n", split, x.size(0), f.size(1));
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| pool | images | image geometry | factor columns |
|---|---:|---|---:|
| fit | 210 | 28x28x1 | 4 |
| validation | 42 | 28x28x1 | 4 |
| test | 42 | 28x28x1 | 4 |
// result_end

\caption(The native cache supplies the original exhaustive lattice, with no external checkout or Python preparation.)

Seeds E=3301, G=3307 and D=3313 create 6+4+4 leaves and 12,696+13,408+6,289=32,393 scalars.
BatchOrder(210,32,3373) gives seven minibatches per epoch, including an 18-image final batch.
Three epochs therefore perform 21 D, 21 E and 21 G steps: **63 optimizer updates**. Each group
has its own Adam state, rate 0.003, moments 0.9/0.999 and epsilon 1e-8. D updates first, then
E is recomputed with current D, then G is recomputed with current D and E. Group isolation
uses selected leaves; it does not detach the discriminator's input Jacobian.

The fixed four-draw posterior banks use seeds 3323/3329/3335 and independent prior banks
3347/3353/3359 for fit/validation/test. Prior-only generation uses 3371. Fresh epoch posterior
banks use 3390–3392; fresh prior banks use 3408–3410. Float64 MT19937/Box–Muller banks and their
Float32 casts are both retained. All eligible completed epochs 1–3 are scored on fixed
four-draw validation **pixel MSE**, avoiding selection by a changing discriminator metric.
The selected checkpoint restores all three groups into a fresh model. It is model-only restore,
not an optimizer-resume checkpoint. The adapters below only package outputs and checkpoints;
the actual forward, objective selection, differentiation and Adam step are visible in the loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace ae {
void Require(bool ok, const std::string& why) {
  if (!ok)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double a, double b, double tolerance, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(a - b) <= tolerance, why);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
nn::Tensor Flatten(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  return x.reshape({x.size(0), 784});
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays, const std::string& name) {
  for (const auto& [key, value] : arrays)
    if (key == name)
      return value;
  throw std::runtime_error("Missing array:" + name);
}
std::string Bytes(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  const auto v = x.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  return std::string(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(v.data()), v.size() * sizeof(float));
}
bool SameBytes(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::equal_bits(a, b);
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b, int count) {
  return nn::max(nn::abs(nn::slice_axis(Flatten(a), 0, 0, 1) - nn::slice_axis(Flatten(b), 0, 0, 1)))
      .item();
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  return nn::cast(nn::mean(nn::cast(Flatten(x), nn::DType::Float64), {0}), nn::DType::Float32);
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int count) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(row.reshape({1, 784}), {count, 784}).contiguous();
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(Flatten(a), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(Flatten(b), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}
std::vector<BetaFactorData> LoadBetaFactors(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  const auto                  arrays    = nn::load_npz((root / "factors.npz").string());
  const auto                  canonical = nn::models::KnownFactorLattice();
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> result;
  std::set<int>               seen;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"}) {
    const int  count = split == "fit" ? 210 : 42;
    const auto raw = Find(arrays, split + "_images"), factors = Find(arrays, split + "_factors"),
               source = Find(arrays, split + "_source_ids");
    Require(
        raw.shape() == nn::Shape{count, 28, 28, 1} && factors.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32 &&
            factors.shape() == nn::Shape{count, 4} && source.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32 &&
            source.shape() == nn::Shape{count},
        "complete factor-pool schema");
    const auto                known = Find(canonical, split + "_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
    std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
    for (int id : source.to_vector<int>()) {
      auto where = std::find(known.begin(), known.end(), id);
      Require(
          where != known.end() && seen.insert(id).second,
          "unique source ID in correct compositional split");
      rows.push_back(where - known.begin());
    }
    const auto pixels = nn::take_rows(Find(canonical, split + "_images"), rows);
    Require(
        nn::equal_bits(factors, nn::take_rows(Find(canonical, split + "_factors"), rows)),
        "all original factor coordinates");
    Require(
        nn::equal_bits(nn::cast(raw, nn::DType::Float32), pixels),
        "all294x784 pixels match the canonical lattice");
    result.push_back({pixels, factors, source});
  }
  Require(seen.size() == 294, "exhaustive lattice");
  return result;
}
void SaveFactorData(const std::filesystem::path& root, const std::vector<BetaFactorData>& pools) {
  nn::NamedTensors arrays;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string s = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_images", pools[k].images);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_factors", pools[k].factors);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_source_ids", pools[k].source);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "data.npz").string(), arrays);
}
VaeNoiseBank BetaVaeNoise(std::int64_t count, std::int64_t draws, std::uint32_t seed) {
  auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({count, 4}, draws, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor BetaVaeNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& bank, std::int64_t k) {
  return nn::select(bank.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}
using nn::models::VaeGan;
using nn::models::VaeGanDecode;
using nn::models::VaeGanOutput;
class VaeGanModel {
 public:
  nn::ParameterStore encoder{3301}, generator{3307}, discriminator{3313};

  VaeGanModel() {
    {
      nn::NoGradGuard guard;
      VaeGan(
          encoder,
          generator,
          discriminator,
          nn::zeros({1, 784}),
          nn::zeros({1, 4}),
          nn::zeros({1, 4}));
    }
  }
  std::vector<nn::ParameterStore*> Groups() { return {&encoder, &generator, &discriminator}; }
  std::int64_t Count() { return encoder.count() + generator.count() + discriminator.count(); }
  std::size_t  Tensors() { return encoder.size() + generator.size() + discriminator.size(); }

  VaeGanOutput Forward(const nn::Tensor& x, const nn::Tensor& e, const nn::Tensor& p) {
    return VaeGan(encoder, generator, discriminator, Flatten(x), e, p);
  }
  static nn::Tensor Objective(const VaeGanOutput& o, int group) {
    return group == 0 ? o.encoder_loss : group == 1 ? o.generator_loss : o.discriminator_loss;
  }
  /// Named fields of tflow's Evaluate, all checked finite.
  nn::NamedTensors Evaluate(const nn::Tensor& x, const nn::Tensor& e, const nn::Tensor& p) {
    nn::NoGradGuard  guard;
    auto             o = Forward(x, e, p);
    nn::NamedTensors out{
        {"mu", o.mu},
        {"log_variance", o.log_variance},
        {"z", o.z},
        {"probability", o.probability},
        {"prior_probability", o.prior_probability},
        {"real_feature", o.real_feature},
        {"reconstruction_feature", o.reconstruction_feature},
        {"prior_feature", o.prior_feature},
        {"real_logit", o.real_logit},
        {"reconstruction_logit", o.reconstruction_logit},
        {"prior_logit", o.prior_logit},
        {"feature_nll", o.feature_nll},
        {"kl", o.kl},
        {"pixel_nll", o.pixel_nll},
        {"mse", o.mse},
        {"encoder_loss", o.encoder_loss},
        {"generator_loss", o.generator_loss},
        {"discriminator_loss", o.discriminator_loss},
        {"generator_adversarial", o.generator_adversarial}};
    for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
      t = t.contiguous();
      for (float v : t.to_vector<float>())
        Require(std::isfinite(v), "all VAE-GAN fields finite");
    }
    return out;
  }
  /// Isolated group gradient named "<group>/<name>".
  nn::NamedTensors
  Gradient(int group, const nn::Tensor& x, const nn::Tensor& e, const nn::Tensor& p) {
    auto*            store = Groups()[group];
    auto             g     = nn::grad(Objective(Forward(x, e, p), group), store->parameters());
    nn::NamedTensors out;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < g.size(); ++i)
      out.emplace_back(std::to_string(group) + "/" + store->names()[i], g[i]);
    return out;
  }
  /// All arrays named "<k>/<name>" (k = 0 encoder, 1 generator, 2 discriminator).
  nn::NamedTensors Arrays() {
    nn::NamedTensors out;
    auto             stores = Groups();
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : stores[k]->names())
        out.emplace_back(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, stores[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
    return out;
  }
  std::vector<std::string> Snapshot() {
    std::vector<std::string> out;
    for (const auto& [key, value] : Arrays())
      out.push_back(Bytes(value));
    return out;
  }
  /// Loads "<k>/<name>" arrays (tflow's initial_arrays.npz / our best.npz).
  void Load(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays) {
    Require(arrays.size() == Tensors(), "all VAE-GAN tensors supplied");
    auto stores = Groups();
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : stores[k]->names()) {
        auto value = Find(arrays, std::to_string(k) + "/" + name);
        Require(value.shape() == stores[k]->at(name).shape(), "matching VAE-GAN shapes");
        stores[k]->set(name, value.contiguous().clone());
      }
  }
  /// Code-only generation.
  nn::Tensor Decode(const nn::Tensor& z) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    return VaeGanDecode(generator, z).contiguous();
  }
};

std::vector<double> VaeGanScore(
    VaeGanModel&        model,
    const nn::Tensor&   images,
    const VaeNoiseBank& noise,
    const VaeNoiseBank& prior) {
  std::vector<double> total(4);
  for (int draw = 0; draw < 4; ++draw) {
    const auto fields =
        model.Evaluate(images, BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise, draw), BetaVaeNoiseAt(prior, draw));
    int index = 0;
    for (const std::string key : {"mse", "pixel_nll", "feature_nll", "kl"})
      total[index++] += nn::sum(nn::cast(Find(fields, key), nn::DType::Float64)).item();
  }
  for (auto& value : total)
    value /= double(4 * images.size(0));
  return total;
}
} // namespace ae
namespace check {
using ae::Near;
using ae::Require;
} // namespace check
namespace {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  auto pools = ae::LoadBetaFactors(data);
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  ae::SaveFactorData(root, pools);
  std::vector<ae::VaeNoiseBank> noise, priors;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    noise.push_back(ae::BetaVaeNoise(pools[k].images.size(0), 4, 3323 + k * 6));
    priors.push_back(ae::BetaVaeNoise(pools[k].images.size(0), 4, 3347 + k * 6));
  }
  nn::NamedTensors banks;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    banks.emplace_back(split + "_epsilon", noise[k].epsilon);
    banks.emplace_back(split + "_standard", noise[k].standard);
    banks.emplace_back(split + "_prior_epsilon", priors[k].epsilon);
    banks.emplace_back(split + "_prior_standard", priors[k].standard);
  }
  auto prior_noise = ae::BetaVaeNoise(20, 1, 3371);
  banks.emplace_back("generation_standard", prior_noise.standard);
  banks.emplace_back("generation_epsilon", prior_noise.epsilon);
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), banks);
  ae::VaeGanModel     model;
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  std::vector<std::unique_ptr<nn::Optimizer>> optimizers;
  for (auto* group : model.Groups())
    optimizers.push_back(std::make_unique<nn::Optimizer>(*group, .003, config));
  if (!init.empty())
    model.Load(nn::load_npz(init));
  const std::int64_t parameters = model.Count();
  const std::size_t  tensors    = model.Tensors();
  check::Require(parameters == 32393 && tensors == 14, "compact VAE-GAN census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), model.Arrays());
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 3373);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history
      << "epoch\tvalidation_mc_mse\tvalidation_pixel_nll\tvalidation_feature_nll\tvalidation_kl\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, steps = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    auto train = ae::BetaVaeNoise(210, 1, 3389 + epoch),
         prior = ae::BetaVaeNoise(210, 1, 3407 + epoch);
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", train.standard},
         {"epsilon", train.epsilon},
         {"prior_standard", prior.standard},
         {"prior_epsilon", prior.epsilon}});
    auto e = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(train, 0), p = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(prior, 0);
    order.begin_epoch();
    int seen = 0;
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), epsilon = nn::take_rows(e, rows),
           z = nn::take_rows(p, rows);
      if (!steps) {
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_batch.npz").string(),
            {{"images", x}, {"epsilon", epsilon}, {"prior", z}});
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), model.Evaluate(x, epsilon, z));
        for (int group = 0; group < 3; ++group)
          nn::save_npz(
              (root / ("initial_gradients_group" + std::to_string(group) + ".npz")).string(),
              model.Gradient(group, x, epsilon, z));
      }
      for (int group : {2, 0, 1}) {
        const auto before = steps ? nn::NamedTensors{} : model.Arrays();
        if (!steps)
          nn::save_npz(
              (root / ("first_actual_gradients_group" + std::to_string(group) + ".npz")).string(),
              model.Gradient(group, x, epsilon, z));
        // Recompute from CURRENT D/E/G weights before EACH isolated update.
        const auto forward = nn::models::VaeGan(
            model.encoder, model.generator, model.discriminator, ae::Flatten(x), epsilon, z);
        const auto   objective = group == 0   ? forward.encoder_loss
                                 : group == 1 ? forward.generator_loss
                                              : forward.discriminator_loss;
        const double loss      = objective.item<float>();
        const auto   gradients = nn::grad(objective, model.Groups()[group]->parameters());
        for (const auto& gradient : gradients)
          for (double value : gradient.to_vector<double>())
            ae::Require(std::isfinite(value), "finite phase derivative");
        optimizers[group]->step(gradients);
        check::Require(
            std::isfinite(loss) && loss >= 0, "all three nonnegative finite training objectives");
        if (!steps) {
          auto after   = model.Arrays();
          bool changed = false;
          for (const auto& [key, value] : before) {
            const bool same = nn::equal_bits(value, ae::Find(after, key));
            if (key[0] - '0' == group)
              changed |= !same;
            else
              check::Require(same, "isolated update changes ONLY intended variable group");
          }
          check::Require(changed, "intended group actually updates");
          nn::save_npz(
              (root / ("first_after_group" + std::to_string(group) + ".npz")).string(), after);
        }
      }
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      ++steps;
      seen += int(rows.size());
    }
    check::Require(seen == 210, "all fit cases once per epoch");
    auto score = ae::VaeGanScore(model, pools[1].images, noise[1], priors[1]);
    history << epoch;
    for (auto v : score)
      history << '\t' << v;
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), model.Arrays());
    if (score[0] < best) {
      best     = score[0];
      selected = epoch;
      nn::save_npz(best_path, model.Arrays()); // validation MC pixel MSE selects all THREE groups
    }
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();

  ae::VaeGanModel deployed;
  deployed.Load(nn::load_npz(best_path)); // fresh all-group model-only restore
  check::Near(
      ae::VaeGanScore(deployed, pools[1].images, noise[1], priors[1])[0],
      best,
      1e-9,
      "restored selection score");
  const auto       before = deployed.Snapshot();
  nn::NamedTensors outputs;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string  split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    const std::int64_t n     = pools[k].images.size(0);
    auto               mean =
        deployed.Evaluate(pools[k].images, nn::zeros({n, 4}), ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[k], 0));
    check::Require(
        ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(mean, "mu"), ae::Find(mean, "z")),
        "zero epsilon gives posterior mu");
    for (const auto& [key, v] : mean)
      outputs.emplace_back(split + "_zero_" + key, v);
    for (int draw = 0; draw < 4; ++draw) {
      auto f = deployed.Evaluate(
          pools[k].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[k], draw), ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[k], draw));
      for (const auto& [key, v] : f)
        outputs.emplace_back(split + "_draw" + std::to_string(draw) + "_" + key, v);
    }
  }
  auto e = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 0), p = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[2], 0);
  auto test   = deployed.Evaluate(pools[2].images, e, p),
       repeat = deployed.Evaluate(pools[2].images, e, p),
       other  = deployed.Evaluate(pools[2].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 1), p);
  check::Require(
      ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(test, "probability"), ae::Find(repeat, "probability")) &&
          ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(test, "probability"), deployed.Decode(ae::Find(test, "z"))),
      "repeat and code-only decode BITEXACT");
  check::Require(
      !ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(test, "z"), ae::Find(other, "z")) &&
          !ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(test, "probability"), ae::Find(other, "probability")) &&
          ae::SameBytes(ae::Find(test, "mu"), ae::Find(other, "mu")),
      "noise affects latent/probability,not encoder heads");
  auto single = deployed.Evaluate(
      nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0}), nn::take_rows(e, {0}), nn::take_rows(p, {0}));
  const double parity =
      ae::MaxAbsDiff(ae::Find(single, "probability"), ae::Find(test, "probability"), 784);
  check::Require(parity < 2e-6, "single/batch parity");
  auto prior_z = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(prior_noise, 0), prior = deployed.Decode(prior_z);
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), {{"z", prior_z}, {"probability", prior}});
  check::Require(before == deployed.Snapshot(), "all inference leaves THREE groups unchanged");
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), deployed.Arrays());
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), outputs);
  auto         score    = ae::VaeGanScore(deployed, pools[2].images, noise[2], priors[2]);
  auto         mean     = ae::Constant(ae::PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const double mse      = ae::Mse(ae::Find(outputs, "test_zero_probability"), pools[2].images),
               baseline = ae::Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":" << parameters << ",\"tensors\":" << tensors << ",\"epochs\":" << epochs
       << ",\"steps_per_group\":" << steps << ",\"total_optimizer_updates\":" << 3 * steps
       << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected << ",\"mc_samples\":4,\"test_mc_mse\":" << score[0]
       << ",\"test_diagnostic_pixel_nll\":" << score[1] << ",\"test_feature_nll\":" << score[2]
       << ",\"test_kl\":" << score[3] << ",\"decode_mu_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"fit_mean_mse\":" << baseline << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";

  check::Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete VAE-GAN evidence");
  std::print(
      "| selected epoch | test MC pixel MSE | diagnostic pixel NLL | feature residual | KL | "
      "decode(mu) MSE | fitting mean MSE |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| {} | {:.9f} | "
      "{:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      selected,
      score[0],
      score[1],
      score[2],
      score[3],
      mse,
      baseline);
}
} // namespace
int main() {
  try {
    const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets");
    Run(std::filesystem::path(cache) / "beta_vae", "build/vae_gan", 3, "");
    return 0;
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}
```
