\caption(Epoch 3 is selected. The MC metrics average Float32 per-image terms over four fixed draws using Float64 accumulation; decode(mu) and the fitting-mean reference use Float64 pixel reductions.)

All 24 parameter/noise/forward archives and complete histories match the source bit for bit.
The two summary MSEs use tensor Float64 pixel reductions instead of the source's host sum;
the observed differences are below 1.1e-14. Every other non-timing JSON value remains exact.

> Selection and the first three isolated updates

Only validation pixel MSE selects the checkpoint. No test value is consulted during fitting.
Feature-loss values at different epochs also reflect changes in D; they are not measurements
under a fixed perceptual metric.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vae_gan_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream input("build/vae_gan/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(input, header);
  std::vector<double> epochs, mse;
  double              e, m, p, f, k;
  while (input >> e >> m >> p >> f >> k) {
    epochs.push_back(e);
    mse.push_back(m);
  }
  if (epochs.size() != 3)
    return 1;
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(epochs, mse, "validation", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(epochs, mse, "", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .title("Fixed four-draw validation / select pixel MSE")
      .x_label("completed epoch / all three eligible")
      .y_label("mean squared pixel error")
      .y_limits(.247,.2502)
      .y_ticks({.247,.248,.249,.250},{"0.247","0.248","0.249","0.250"})
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"1", "2", "3"})
      .save_svg("build/vae_gan_validation.svg");
}
