\caption(Only the chosen group's parameters change in each first step. E and G use recomputed gradients that differ from the initial snapshot; D starts from that snapshot.)

The selected model has test MC pixel MSE 0.247712397, diagnostic pixel NLL 539.843249730,
feature residual 5.041923702 and KL 0.471085257. Decode(mu) MSE is 0.245177199, while the
fitting-only pixel mean gives 0.048548290. This short run does not beat that simple baseline.
A small learned feature residual is not evidence of better images, a normalized image
likelihood, useful semantics or an improvement over a matched trained VAE control.

> Unfiltered held-out reconstruction and code-only generation

Each row below is original, decode(mu), one posterior probability draw and fitting-only mean.
The ten rows are evenly spaced in source order; they are not selected for visual quality.
Decode(mu) is not a posterior predictive mean. All rendered images are sigmoid probabilities,
not Bernoulli pixel samples, with a shared fixed 0–1 grayscale.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vae_gan_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  auto data    = n::load_npz("build/vae_gan/data.npz"),
       outputs = n::load_npz("build/vae_gan/outputs.npz");
  auto find    = [](const n::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  const auto fit  = find(data, "fit_images").reshape({210, 784});
  const auto mean = n::cast(n::mean(n::cast(fit, n::DType::Float64), {0}), n::DType::Float32);
  const std::vector<n::Tensor> values{
      find(data, "test_images").reshape({42, 784}),
      find(outputs, "test_zero_probability"),
      find(outputs, "test_draw0_probability"),
      n::broadcast_to(mean.reshape({1, 784}), {42, 784})};
  std::vector<n::Tensor> rows;
  const auto             ids = find(data, "test_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
  std::print("Displayed source IDs:");
  for (int k = 0; k < 10; ++k) {
    const int row = k * 41 / 9;
    std::print(" {}", ids[row]);
    for (const auto& value : values)
      rows.push_back(n::take_rows(value, {row}));
  }
  std::print(".\n");
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(rows, 0).reshape({40, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/vae_gan_reconstructions.png",
      4,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220. / 255.,
      3);
}
